{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9y9ZxWnK1F9DZEL6m2G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--and` patterns now get the same path-separator check as the primary pattern. All tests pass and clippy is clean.\n\n- **`src/main.rs`:** I moved the existing check into a new function, `ensure_pattern_is_not_a_path(pattern)`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs it on the primary pattern and then on every `--and` pattern. It still skips everything when `--full-path` is set. The error message is unchanged, except that it now names whichever pattern has the separator.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** I added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`, which checks that `fd foo --and one/two` fails with the error.\n\nThe Windows-only `\\` branch now covers `--and` patterns too, but this machine runs Linux, so that branch wasn't compiled or tested here. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":511,"cache_read_input_tokens":36540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":511,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76040828-2dc7-4135-af02-baf4f4563902","uuid":"50b08374-7be7-4110-8300-6222754a9a1f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:51:00.539Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9y9ZjcZRj8xf27yjo27"}
